{
  "rationale": "The plant models robot perception and motion capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and actuation (controllable). The specification binds sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery only when obstacles are detected and returning to exploration as soon as possible. Helper states ensure one-shot actions and correct event sequencing.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion to reflect open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-maximizing exploration with conservative obstacle recovery, ensuring only one controllable per state and deterministic transitions."
  ],
